# Execution verification

- Repository release-focused selection: 524 tests, zero failures/errors, 42 skips.
- Installed snapshot selected functional tests: 261 tests, all pass, zero skips.
- npm global selected socket/control/lifecycle tests: 52 tests, all pass.
- Installed snapshot native Claude and Codex remote each passed scoped restart
  acceptance: old child exit, replacement, resumed session and new input replied.
  Claude uncertain attempts remained fenced and not replayed. Codex app-server
  port release observed. No probe-timeout monkeypatch was used in installed runs.
- Owned test listeners absent after cleanup. Text console captures and lifecycle
  logs retained locally; window screenshot capture was unavailable (0x0 window).
- SSE fixture independently verifies two real listener outages/restorations,
  cursor continuation, one worker, and actual HTTP controls to durable gateway
  input. This is not a single native CLI + network-outage scenario.

# Limits and corrections

- Original reported URLError root cause remains unknown; real NIC/VPN/DNS flap
  recovery is not established by loopback fixture.
- Additional raw-console typing after restart failed in earlier diagnostic runs;
  this release does not claim that separate path fixed.
- Initial d59c7a1 CI/Publish failed due to Linux-specific OSError(111) subclass
  construction in a new test. Corrected by explicit ConnectionRefusedError in
  4907ba8, then both exact-SHA workflows passed. No CI failure was waived.
- A verification shell attempted PowerShell variable syntax through Bash; that
  assignment failed. Identity/hash/tests were subsequently verified directly
  against installed absolute roots, without depending on that assignment.
- Alibaba token-plan-only error report is a separate unverified issue; screenshot
  unavailable to current provider. No causal link to SSE is claimed.
